urce):\n\n| Setting | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `codex-worker` | terra | default |\n| `codex-reviewer` | astra | project |\n| `claude-worker` | sonnet | default |\n| `claude-reviewer` | opus | default |\n| `worker-effort` | high | default |\n| `review-effort` | xhigh | default |\n\n`codex-reviewer` is `astra`. It's set at the project level, which overrides the global setting and the `sol` default.\n\nSettings resolve in this order: `CXC_*` env var, then project, then Claude Code `/config`, then global, then default. To change one, use `peer-coding:mode <setting> <value>`, adding `--global` for every project. You can also use `/config` and search for \"peer-coding\".","ttft_ms":1951,"type":"result","duration_ms":7649,"uuid":"7dadb26c-d038-4104-8a7b-7084112ed84d","ttft_stream_ms":1009,"time_to_request_ms":154,"first_content_frame_ms":1009,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
